From 4a85bc7adb0771c1f01a3782a7d2c22a4486fcc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:02:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] GBLink: real GBAs over JOY Bus (test firmware), local and
 netplay

A new SI device forwards each JOY Bus command to a GBA on a GB-Link adapter in
the firmware's GameCube mode (0x08), so the GBA runs its own cartridge and no
GBA is emulated. In netplay the port's owner sends each reply to the room and
the other machines wait for it. Traffic and wait times go to GBLink.log.
Also detects firmware 3.0.0 adapters (USB ID 1209:B011).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
